# Supabase Patterns

## Client
- Single client instance in `src/lib/supabase.ts` — never create new clients elsewhere
- Typed as `createClient<any>` — use explicit type casts in services (`as Book`, `as Profile[]`)

## Service Pattern
```ts
// ✅ Every method: query → check error → cast and return
async getBooks(filters: BookFilters): Promise<Book[]> {
  const { data, error } = await supabase.from("books").select("*");
  if (error) throw error;
  return (data ?? []) as Book[];
}
```

## Joins
Use PostgREST dot-notation for joins — always alias with the relation name:
```ts
// books with genre, borrow_records with book + member
.select(`*, genre:genres(id, name, created_at)`)
.select(`*, book:books(id, title, author), member:profiles(id, full_name, email)`)
```

## Inventory RPC Functions (atomic, use these — never raw UPDATE for copies)
| Function | When to call |
|---|---|
| `borrow_book(p_book_id)` | Member borrows — decrements `available_copies` |
| `return_book(p_book_id)` | Member returns — increments `available_copies` |
| `reserve_book(p_book_id)` | Librarian reserves — decrements `available_copies` (holds copy) |
| `release_reservation(p_book_id)` | Reservation cancelled — increments `available_copies` |

```ts
const { error } = await supabase.rpc("borrow_book", { p_book_id: bookId });
if (error) throw error;
```

## RLS Summary
- `profiles`: own row read/write; librarians read all
- `books / genres`: all authenticated users read; librarians write
- `borrow_records`: members read own; librarians read + write all
- `reservations`: members read own; librarians manage all
- `notifications`: users read + mark-read own; librarians insert

## Migrations
- Files in `supabase/migrations/` named `NNN_description.sql`
- Current files: `001_initial_schema`, `002_seed_genres`, `003_rpc_functions`
- All new tables must include `alter table ... enable row level security`
- All new inventory-affecting operations need an RPC function — no raw copy updates from the client

## Auth Flow
- Sign up → Supabase creates `auth.users` → trigger `handle_new_user()` auto-creates `profiles` row with `role = 'member'`
- Promote to librarian: manually set `profiles.role = 'librarian'` in Supabase dashboard
- `get_my_role()` SQL function used inside RLS policies — do not remove it
